---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  room="paper"
  title="Privacy — Latent"
  description="Privacy should be simple. Latent collects as little as possible, uses it only when necessary, and never sells your information."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="legal" id="main">
    <div class="legal-label">Privacy</div>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated 12 September 2026</p>

    <p class="legal-lead">Privacy should be simple. We collect as little as possible, use it only when necessary, and never sell your information.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>You can browse this website without creating an account. We use no advertising, no analytics, and no tracking cookies. As with any internet service, our hosting provider processes ordinary request and security information, such as your IP address, browser details, requested page, and time of access, to deliver and protect the service.</p>
    <p>We ask for your email address only when it is needed for something you choose to do: subscribe to the newsletter, contact us, or complete a purchase through Paddle.</p>

    <h2>The newsletter</h2>
    <p>If you subscribe, your email address is managed by Buttondown, our email provider, and used only to send occasional updates about Latent.</p>
    <p>Every email includes an unsubscribe link, and you can leave at any time.</p>

    <h2>Latent accounts and Manager</h2>
    <p>Latent Manager lets you sign in with Google or Apple so one Latent account can hold your products and restore them on an authorized Mac. The sign-in provider confirms who you are and gives us a provider-specific identifier. We protect that identifier before storing it; we do not receive or store your Google or Apple password, and we do not use your provider email address as a hidden account-merging key.</p>
    <p>We keep an internal account identifier, the providers you connect, the preferred name you enter, installation identifiers, protected session records, and the dates needed to operate and secure the account. Sign-in challenges are short-lived, session secrets are stored only as protected hashes on our service, and the usable session token is kept in your Mac&rsquo;s Keychain.</p>

    <h2>Licensing and installations</h2>
    <p>To activate, restore, and verify a product, we keep the minimum license record needed for that purpose: your internal Latent account identifier, product and plan, license status and relevant dates, Paddle customer, transaction, or subscription identifiers where a purchase is involved, and an installation public key and fingerprint for each authorized Mac. We also keep cryptographic hashes and audit records that let us issue, refresh, revoke, and defend a license without storing its private installation key.</p>
    <p>Your Mac creates and keeps its private installation key locally. Latent does not receive it. The licensing system never receives your photographs, footage, project files, or payment card details.</p>

    <h2>Your photographs</h2>
    <p>Latent is a darkroom, not a cloud service.</p>
    <p>Your photographs remain on your device. We do not receive, store, or have access to them &mdash; with one exception: work you deliberately publish through a Latent app&rsquo;s community, described below.</p>
    <p>If you choose to use iCloud Photos or iCloud Drive, that synchronization is provided by Apple through your own account and remains under your control.</p>

    <h2>The Moment and The Ritual community</h2>
    <p>The Moment and Latent The Ritual offer the same two ways to share, and both are opt-in. Nothing is shared unless you choose to share it.</p>
    <p>A <strong>Circle</strong> is a small, private shared album. Everything a Circle holds &mdash; its members, photographs, videos, notes, and keeps &mdash; is looked after by Latent&rsquo;s own community service, and only the people invited into that Circle can see it. Like any shared album that delivers photographs between phones, the service can read what it carries; ordinary Circle content is private to its members, not encrypted end-to-end.</p>
    <p><strong>Envelopes</strong> &mdash; the Circle&rsquo;s private messages &mdash; are sealed on the sender&rsquo;s device before they travel. Our service delivers them without holding the keys; only Circle members can open them.</p>
    <p>The <strong>Field</strong> is the public space shared by The Moment and The Ritual. Joining it creates a community account with a handle and a display name, and anything you publish there &mdash; photographs, titles, captions, notes &mdash; becomes visible to other members, associated with your handle. Latent&rsquo;s community service keeps only what the feature needs: your account, your profile, what you publish, and the notes, keeps, appreciations, and follows you place.</p>
    <p>Field and Circle content is stored by Latent&rsquo;s community service on Cloudflare. It is not stored in iCloud and does not use your iCloud space.</p>
    <p>Photographs you publish carry no location data, even if location was recorded when they were taken &mdash; that stays on your device.</p>
    <p>If you turn on community notifications, your device&rsquo;s delivery address for them (its push token) is registered with our service and used only for delivery. If you report content or a member, the report comes to us and is used only to look after the community. Blocking someone is remembered so their work stays out of your view.</p>
    <p>You can take back a published post at any time, close a Circle you own, leave a Circle, and delete your community account entirely from inside the app. What you take back is removed from our service; a copy someone already saved to their own device is beyond our reach &mdash; as with anything shared.</p>

    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>Purchases made on this website are processed by Paddle.com, our online reseller and Merchant of Record. Paddle collects what it needs to take payment, issue a receipt, calculate tax, and handle refunds. We never receive your payment card details.</p>
    <p>Paddle may share with us your name, email address, country, and what you bought, so we can send you the download and support the purchase. We use that only for fulfillment and support. We do not sell it.</p>
    <p>Paddle&rsquo;s own privacy policy applies to the information they collect: <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy">paddle.com/legal/privacy</a></p>
    <p>App Store purchases are still processed by Apple. We never receive those card details either.</p>
    <p>If you want a purchase record deleted, write to us at <a href="mailto:support@latentstudios.art">support@latentstudios.art</a>. Where Paddle holds the record, we will pass the request on.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Short-lived sign-in challenges and expired or revoked sessions are removed automatically after limited security and recovery periods. We keep account and licensing records while your account or license remains active, and keep transaction or audit records as reasonably necessary to honor ownership, prevent fraud and replay, handle refunds or disputes, and meet legal obligations.</p>

    <h2>Services we rely on</h2>
    <p>We keep our tools few.</p>
    <ul class="legal-list">
      <li>Buttondown for newsletters.</li>
      <li>Google for Sign in with Google.</li>
      <li>Apple for Sign in with Apple, push notifications, App Store services, and any Apple Photos or iCloud features you choose to use. Apple does not host Field or Circle content for Latent.</li>
      <li>Cloudflare, whose infrastructure runs this website and Latent&rsquo;s separate account, licensing, and community services.</li>
      <li>Paddle.com, for website purchases, receipts, tax, and refunds.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each service maintains its own privacy policy.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You may unsubscribe from our newsletter at any time.</p>
    <p>You may also ask to access, correct, or delete personal information we hold by writing to <a href="mailto:support@latentstudios.art">support@latentstudios.art</a>. If deleting an account would also remove the account authority needed to restore or manage a license, we will explain that consequence before carrying out the request.</p>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights over your personal information. We will honor those rights where applicable.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Latent is not intended for children under the age of 16, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, we will update this page and revise the date above.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy? <a href="mailto:support@latentstudios.art">support@latentstudios.art</a></p>

    <a class="legal-back" href="/">← Back to Latent</a>
  </main>
  <Footer />

  <style>
    .legal { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 140px 24px 120px; }
    .legal-label { font-family: var(--font-label); font-weight: 300; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.28em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--amber-dim); margin-bottom: 20px; }
    .legal h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 300; font-size: 40px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--text-bright); margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .legal-updated { font-family: var(--font-body); font-style: italic; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-ghost); margin-bottom: 48px; }
    .legal-lead { font-size: 18px !important; line-height: 1.75 !important; color: var(--text) !important; }
    .legal-list { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 20px; }
    .legal-list li { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 300; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
    .legal h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 400; font-size: 21px; color: var(--text-bright); margin: 40px 0 12px; }
    .legal p { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 300; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .legal a { color: var(--amber); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light); transition: color 0.3s ease, text-shadow 0.6s ease, border-color 0.6s ease; }
    .legal a:hover { color: var(--text-bright); text-shadow: 0 0 16px rgba(232, 196, 160, 0.5); border-color: transparent; }
    .legal-back { display: inline-block; margin-top: 48px; font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--amber-dim); border-bottom: none; }
    .legal-back:hover { color: var(--text-bright); text-shadow: 0 0 16px rgba(232, 196, 160, 0.5); }
  </style>
</Base>
